---
source: crates/rustman-cli/src/tests.rs
expression: help
---
Manage signers: import a key into the OS keychain

Usage: rustman evm signer [OPTIONS] <COMMAND>

Commands:
  import  Store a private key in the OS keychain as signer <ID>
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --color <WHEN>
          Color: auto (a terminal without NO_COLOR or TERM=dumb), always or never
          
          [default: auto]

  -v, --verbose...
          Log more on stderr: -v requests, -vv headers, -vvv everything (RUST_LOG, when set, replaces these levels)

  -h, --help
          Print help

Examples:
  rustman evm signer import deployer
  rustman evm signer import ci < ci.key

The key is read with a no-echo prompt (or from stdin when piped), stored in
the OS keychain, and used from rustman.toml with:
  [evm.signers.<id>]
  keychain = true
